--- /dev/null
+++ b/notes/research.md
@@ -0,0 +1,26 @@
+# Research
+
+## Request paths and current behavior
+
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/api/v1/customer/CustomerApi.java` exposes customer deletion through the customer facade.
+- `sm-core/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/business/services/customer/CustomerServiceImpl.java` deletes the customer and its attributes only. Orders do not have a JPA customer association: `Order.customerId` is a scalar id and `Order.customerEmailAddress`, embedded billing, and embedded delivery are stored on the order.
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/api/v1/order/OrderApi.java` handles the admin routes. `/private/orders/customers/{id}` currently loads `Customer` first and returns 404 when it has been deleted, so it never queries the retained order rows. `/private/orders` builds `OrderCriteria` with page/count and filters and delegates to the facade. `/private/orders/{id}` delegates to the facade.
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/controller/order/facade/OrderFacadeImpl.java` converts repository orders to API orders. Its customer-list overload currently uses the legacy offset/count path. Its admin-list overload returns an empty object with `recordsTotal=0` when a page has no rows, losing the repository total; it otherwise exposes `recordsTotal`, `totalPages`, and current-page counts.
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/controller/order/facade/OrderFacadeImpl.java` gets an order through `OrderService.getOrder`, then attempts to populate the customer separately. If the customer is absent it logs and leaves `ReadableOrder.customer` unset; the order populator still maps billing, delivery, and stored email.
+
+## Repository causes
+
+- `sm-core/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/business/repositories/order/OrderRepository.java` uses inner fetch joins for `merchant`, `orderProducts`, `orderTotal`, and `orderHistory` in `findOne`. A retained order can therefore disappear if any of these collections/associations is absent, independently of customer deletion. The order-detail query should retain orders while using left joins for optional historical data.
+- `sm-core/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/business/repositories/order/OrderRepositoryImpl.java` contains two list implementations. The legacy `listByStore` filters by scalar `o.customerId`, but when `startIndex > 0` sets `maxResults` to `first + max`, which is incorrect for a page size and contributes to broken later pages. The newer `listOrders` supports store, name, email, id, phone, and status filters and sorts by descending id, but `RepositoryHelper.paginateQuery` computes `totalPages` as integer division plus one (wrong for exact multiples), and the response facade drops totals on empty pages.
+- Name/phone predicates are currently concatenated without parentheses (`store AND firstName LIKE ... OR lastName LIKE ...`), so the OR branch can escape the store/filter constraints. This is an affected filtering correctness issue in the same query path.
+- `sm-core-model/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/model/common/EntityList.java` forces a zero `totalPages` value to serialize as one. The requested contract is the mathematical number of pages, including zero for zero matching records, so response construction should set the explicit value rather than relying on this legacy getter behavior where possible.
+
+## Registration and order retention impact
+
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/populator/order/PersistableOrderApiPopulator.java` resolves an existing customer id when supplied and copies that id/email/details into the new order; anonymous registration creates a customer through the normal customer service. No order lookup is by email, so a newly registered customer with a reused email should remain separate as long as customer-order queries use `customerId` only.
+- The existing order model already has the data needed after deletion. The fix must not null or rewrite `Order.customerId`; it should treat that id as historical ownership and make customer enrichment optional.
+
+## Tests and verification options
+
+- Core tests are under `sm-core/src/test`, including `OrderTest` and `CustomerTest`; shop integration tests are under `sm-shop/src/test`, including `OrderApiIntegrationTest` and customer registration coverage.
+- No existing test was found covering deleted-customer order retrieval or admin page navigation. The implementation should add focused repository/service/API-level coverage if the project test setup permits; at minimum compile and run the relevant Maven module tests.
